                <pb facs="0613" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13528: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-11T13:00:00+08:00">June 11, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 11—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>299. Following telegram has been received from the Consul General at Hankow:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 10, 5 p.m. Press reports from Sian state that Reds under Mao
                            Tse-tung, Peng Teh-huai and Hsu Hai-tung have entered Kansu from
                            northwestern Shensi, that on June 4th they were north of Hwanhsien on
                            the Kwan River in eastern Kansu and south of Ting-pien, Shensi and that
                            they would move westwards into Kansu or northwestwards into Ningsia. My
                            latest information is contained in a telegram dated June 10th from
                            Scandinavian Alliance Mission at Pingliang, Kansu, in reply to a
                            telegram from me warning the mission that the Shensi Reds were moving
                            into Kansu; this telegram reads <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘Red movement direction confirmed, main force northward
                                    travelling westward Tsingning, Americans in Pingliang city
                                    safe.’</p>
                            </quote></p>
                        <p rendition="#flush">I have sent telegrams of warning to all Americans
                            known to be in or en route to Kansu or Chinghai.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
